Drop the config machinery this plugin never used

env-file.mjs was inherited from the template and loaded on every import,
but the plugin reads no configuration at all: the factory destructured
env and immediately discarded it with a void statement. A role is a fact
about a live session, held in the registry, so there is nothing to read
from the environment and no .env to load.

The factory now takes only the diagnostic logger, rather than accepting
context it has no use for and voiding it -- which read as though the
values mattered and had merely been forgotten.

The pass-through interceptor raised alongside this is already gone; it
was removed when roles landed. It survives only in the frozen template
commit, whose skeleton needed it because interceptors were once the
smallest registration core would accept. The README now says that
outright, so the next person reading the template knows why it is there
and that it no longer applies.

